  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on variance as a mathematical measure of risk, preferring lower variance. The individual considers the certainty of outcome and avoids the risk of getting nothing, which aligns with preferring lower variability in outcomes. Although the individual does not mention variance explicitly or perform any calculation, their preference for the certain outcome (Lottery B) due to risk and regret avoidance reflects a qualitative sensitivity to outcome dispersion. The core of the decision reason (favoring less variable outcomes) overlaps with the individual’s emphasis on safety and certainty. However, the absence of any reference to statistical variation or comparison of outcome spreads makes it uncertain whether variance was used as a reasoning rule. The justification is more affective and heuristic (avoiding regret, preferring sure gains) than analytical. Therefore, while the behavioral outcome aligns with the decision reason, the cognitive process described does not clearly indicate the use of variance as a decision rule.",
  "final_assessment_score": 40
